The file was already written and verified by the linter. Here's a summary:

**Bug:** `mergeImports` compared URLs with exact string match (`b.url === inc.url`), so `"https://example.com/a"` and `"https://EXAMPLE.com/a"` didn't match — the incoming bookmark was added as a duplicate instead of being merged.

**Fix:** Replaced the exact match with a case-insensitive hostname comparison:

```ts
const match = result.find((b) => {
  try {
    return new URL(b.url).hostname.toLowerCase() === new URL(inc.url).hostname.toLowerCase();
  } catch {
    return b.url === inc.url;
  }
});
```

- Uses `new URL(...).hostname.toLowerCase()` to compare hostnames case-insensitively (URL hostnames are case-insensitive per RFC 4343).
- Falls back to exact string comparison if either string isn't a valid URL (avoids crashing on malformed URLs).
- The rest of the merge logic (union of tags, keeping the existing entry) is unchanged.


